4. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements describe what the EduGenie system should do.
FR1 — User Registration and Login
The system should allow users to:
•	Create an account.
•	Log in securely.
•	Log out.
•	Manage basic profile information.
FR2 — AI Tutor Chat
The system should provide a conversational AI interface where students can:
•	Ask academic questions.
•	Receive explanations from Gemini.
•	Ask follow-up questions.
•	Request simpler or more detailed explanations.
•	Ask for examples and analogies.
Example:
Student: "Explain Newton's second law simply."
EduGenie should provide an understandable explanation and, if requested, examples or practice questions.
________________________________________
FR3 — Personalized Explanation
Students should be able to select their preferred learning level:
•	Beginner
•	Intermediate
•	Advanced
•	Exam-oriented
Gemini should generate explanations appropriate to the selected level.
________________________________________
FR4 — Study Material Upload
Students should be able to upload learning materials such as:
•	PDF documents
•	Text notes
•	Lecture materials
•	Images containing study content
The system should process the uploaded material and allow students to interact with it.
________________________________________
FR5 — AI Summarization
EduGenie should generate:
•	Short summaries
•	Detailed summaries
•	Important points
•	Definitions
•	Key concepts
•	Formula lists where applicable
This allows students to quickly revise lengthy material.
________________________________________
FR6 — Ask Your Notes
Students should be able to ask questions about uploaded material.
For example:
"What are the three causes mentioned in this chapter?"
The system should answer based on the relevant uploaded learning content.
________________________________________
FR7 — Quiz Generation
The system should automatically generate quizzes based on:
•	Subject
•	Topic
•	Difficulty level
•	Uploaded material
Supported question types may include:
•	Multiple-choice questions
•	True/false
•	Fill in the blanks
•	Short-answer questions
________________________________________
FR8 — Quiz Evaluation
After completing a quiz, EduGenie should:
•	Calculate the score.
•	Display correct and incorrect answers.
•	Explain incorrect answers.
•	Track the student's performance.
•	Identify topics requiring additional revision.
________________________________________
FR9 — Flashcard Generation
The system should automatically generate flashcards from:
•	Uploaded notes
•	Selected topics
•	AI-generated summaries
Example:
Front: What is photosynthesis?
Back: The process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy.
________________________________________
FR10 — Progress Tracking
The system should maintain student learning information such as:
•	Quizzes attempted
•	Scores
•	Topics studied
•	Weak topics
•	Completed study sessions
•	Learning progress
A dashboard should display this information in an easy-to-understand format.
________________________________________
FR11 — Personalized Recommendations
Based on student performance, EduGenie should recommend:
•	Topics to revise.
•	Additional questions.
•	Flashcards.
•	Relevant study sessions.
•	Practice quizzes.
For example:
"You scored 45% in Algebra. Would you like a short revision session on quadratic equations?"
________________________________________
FR12 — Study Planner
The system should allow students to enter:
•	Subjects
•	Topics
•	Examination dates
•	Available study hours
EduGenie can then generate a suggested study schedule.
________________________________________
FR13 — Exam Preparation
The system should provide an exam preparation mode that can generate:
•	Mock tests
•	Topic-wise tests
•	Revision questions
•	Important concepts
•	Quick revision notes
________________________________________
5. Non-Functional Requirements
NFR1 — Performance
•	The application should respond to user requests within a reasonable time.
•	Frequently accessed information should load quickly.
•	AI requests should provide clear loading/progress feedback.
NFR2 — Usability
The interface should be:
•	Simple.
•	Student-friendly.
•	Responsive.
•	Easy to navigate.
•	Suitable for users with different levels of technical knowledge.
NFR3 — Security
The system should:
•	Authenticate users securely.
•	Protect user accounts.
•	Secure uploaded study materials.
•	Prevent unauthorized access to personal learning data.
•	Use secure communication between the application and backend services.
NFR4 — Scalability
The architecture should support increasing numbers of:
•	Students
•	Uploaded documents
•	AI requests
•	Quiz attempts
•	Stored learning records
NFR5 — Reliability
The application should handle:
•	Network failures.
•	Invalid files.
•	Gemini API failures.
•	Invalid user inputs.
Appropriate error messages should be displayed rather than causing the application to crash.
NFR6 — Maintainability
The system should use modular components so that features such as voice interaction, additional AI models, or new quiz types can be added later.
NFR7 — Availability
The application should be available whenever students need to access their learning resources, subject to the availability of the underlying cloud and AI services.
